read, the loop body is executed 10 times.\n    - **Conclusion**: The read operation at line 14 is **executable** in subsequent iterations or after preemption.\n\n### Final Defect Report\n\nAll read/write operations listed in the initial defect report are confirmed to be accessible. The control conditions (the `for` loops in both ISRs) are satisfied, allowing the code within them to execute. Given that `svp_simple_330_001_isr_2` has a higher priority than `svp_simple_330_001_isr_1`, it can preempt `isr_1`, leading to the reported interleaving. Therefore, the original report is correct.\n\n```json\n{\n    \"violations\": [\n        {\n            \"sharedVariable\": \"j\",\n            \"accessPattern\": [\"Read\", \"Write\", \"Read\"],\n            \"lines\": [\"14\", \"21\", \"14\"]\n        }\n    ]\n}\n```\n\n[Expert R2] (Refine the report based on judge feedback, re-check for missed or false defects.)\nAbstain\n\n"
