sr_1`.\n- The reported access pattern `Write -> Read -> Write` on variable `i` can occur through the following interleaving:\n    1. `svp_simple_330_001_isr_1` is triggered and executes the write `i = j + 1;` (line 14).\n    2. An interrupt for `svp_simple_330_001_isr_2` occurs, and since it has higher priority, it preempts `isr_1`.\n    3. `svp_simple_330_001_isr_2` executes, performing the read of `i` in the statement `j = i + 1;` (line 21).\n    4. `svp_simple_330_001_isr_2` completes, and execution returns to `svp_simple_330_001_isr_1`.\n    5. `svp_simple_330_001_isr_1` continues its execution, for example, in a subsequent iteration of its loop, and performs another write `i = j + 1;` (line 14).\n\nAll involved operations are accessible, and the preemption model allows for the reported interleaving. Therefore, the atomicity violation is valid.\n\n```json\n{\n    \"violations\": [\n        {\n            \"sharedVariable\": \"i\",\n            \"accessPattern\": [\"Write\", \"Read\", \"Write\"],\n            \"lines\": [14, 21, 14]\n        }\n    ]\n}\n```\n\n[Expert R2] (Refine the report based on judge feedback, re-check for missed or false defects.)\nAbstain\n\n"
